---
title: Book Your First Shipment
description: Create a shipment and track it, with the live API console embedded in the page.
---

This guide books an interstellar shipment with the Shipment API and then tracks it. It is written in Markdoc, so it can use the portal's tags.

{% callout type="tip" title="Try it in the page" %}
The console below is the real Shipment API reference. Fill in the request and choose **Try** to send it to the mock server.
{% /callout %}

## Create the shipment

{% steps %}
{% step title="Get an API key" %}
Create a key in the developer console and send it in the `X-API-Key` header.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Describe the cargo" %}
Send the origin, destination and packages:

{% tabs %}
{% tab name="cURL" %}
```sh
curl -X POST https://api.cosmocargo.dev/v1/shipments \
  -H "X-API-Key: $COSMO_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"origin": "Earth", "destination": "Mars Colony Alpha", "packages": [{"weightKg": 42}]}'
```
{% /tab %}
{% tab name="JavaScript" %}
```js
const response = await fetch('https://api.cosmocargo.dev/v1/shipments', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'X-API-Key': process.env.COSMO_API_KEY, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ origin: 'Earth', destination: 'Mars Colony Alpha', packages: [{ weightKg: 42 }] }),
});
const shipment = await response.json();
```
{% /tab %}
{% /tabs %}
{% /step %}
{% step title="Keep the tracking number" %}
The response contains the `trackingNumber` you need to track the shipment. {% badge text="Required" variant="warning" /%}
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

{% api-operation spec="shipments" path="/shipments" method="post" title="Create a new shipment" /%}

## Track it

{% api-operation spec="shipments" path="/shipments/{trackingNumber}" method="get" title="Track a shipment" /%}

